Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Point the handoff notes at the next task

The status light dashboard is done, so section 5 no longer describes work
that is still pending. It now records what was actually decided about the
percentages, since that decision is easy to overturn by accident and the
numbers stop meaning what they say if it is.

The data section carries the two feed_status traps that cost real analysis
time this round: description-only rows that look like duplicates but are
one fifth of the real events, and the previous_status back-fill that is
only trustworthy inside a single session. Both are the kind of thing that
would otherwise be rediscovered the hard way.

Section 6 gains the lesson behind both - query the real database before
trusting a design assumption - and the note that a new chart page has to be
registered in seven files.

